spes: temperatures and clock, read only (0218, spestherm=N; sub-agent draft, docs/SPES-THERM-DRAFT.md).

bsd/dev/spes_therm.c/.h: TSENS (live DT reg 0x4410000 SROT / 0x4411000 TM, 16 sensors, Linux tsens2xxx), PM6125 RTC second
counter (SID 0 0x6048.., Linux rtc-pm8xxx/qpnp-rtc) and the PMIC temp alarm (0x2400), one log line every 30 s. Stage 2 adds a
read-only dump of the ADC block 0x3100 and its arbiter owner. Stages 3/4 (ADC conversions, Linux qcom-spmi-adc5) need writes to
SID 0 0x3142..0x3147, which this patch does NOT allow-list: sweet_spmi_write() refuses them and the driver says so once.
sweet_spmi_read() gains the read list spes_therm_spmi_read_allowed() (observer reads). Nothing runs without the boot-arg.
Not run on hardware yet; open checks in the draft document.

